    "opencode-v2-service": {
      "protocol": "opencode-v2",
      "note": "Current local service discovery or explicit remote endpoint; Cognia does not stop a service it does not own.",
      "capabilities": {}
    }
  },
  "capabilityNotes": {
    "thinking": "For an external agent this asks whether the HOST can set the thinking / reasoning level, which is the only question any surface acts on. An agent that merely streams thought chunks (every ACP agent) does not satisfy it -- there is nothing to configure. Codex takes it on its options channel and Pi has `set_thinking_level`, so those two are `native`. OpenCode expresses the same idea as variants -- named request overlays for one model, its docs' words -- so v2 is `equivalent`, not `native`: `opencode-v2-client.ts` sends the chosen id as the `variant` half of the `ModelRef` on `session.switchModel`, which is the `provider/model#variant` reference OpenCode itself documents.",
    "mcp": "Whether Cognia can attach an MCP server to the running conversation. ACP carries per-session servers, Codex uses per-thread config, DeepSeek Harness mounts a session-owned composition, and Pi uses the bundled Cognia extension. Remote A2A has no reverse tool channel. OpenCode uses a private local service per conversation; shared remote endpoints cannot attach the local bridge.",
    "session.resume": "Reopening a prior session. On ACP this is gated on the agent advertising stable `sessionCapabilities.resume`, with legacy `loadSession` as a fallback, so the row is `unknown` and the handshake answers it.",
    "compaction": "ACP has no compaction method: the only route is a `/compact` or `/compress` the agent chose to advertise, which is a per-session live fact. Pi and Codex have native methods.",
    "hooks.lifecycle": "Cognia hooks are a host facility, independent of the external protocol. Renderer and CLI dispatch prompt, stream, error and usage hooks around external turns and pre/post hooks around Cognia-projected tools. Native third-party tools remain under the external runtime; the scoped host fact reports whether the Cognia hook runtime is available."
  }
}
